<title>USA: Microtest to cut jobs, restructure.</title>
<headline>Microtest to cut jobs, restructure.</headline>
<dateline>PHOENIX 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Microtest Inc said Friday that it has restructured its sales and marketing operations and expects to save about $4.5 million in fiscal 1997 as a result.</p>
<p>The company also said it cut 45 jobs during the first quarter to eliminate duplication resulting from the acquisition of Logicraft Information Systems last December, and said it is &quot;arranging appropriate severance packages where necessary.&quot;</p>
<p>A spokesman for the company could not say how many severance packages would be offered. The company said it will take an unspecified charge in the first quarter to reflect the severance packages.</p>
<p>Microtest makes diagnostic certification and CD-connectivity products for local area networks and enterprise networks.</p>
</text>
